  "title": "Simón Bolívar",
  "summary": "Simón Bolívar was born in Caracas in 1783 and led campaigns against Spanish rule that helped create Gran Colombia and several South American republics. Called El Libertador, he held high office in Gran Colombia and Peru, and resigned in 1830. He died that year near Santa Marta; admirers and critics weigh his achievements against his authoritarian rule.",
